@page /about
@mode SSG

<div class="page-intro"><a class="breadcrumb" href="../">← OVERVIEW</a><p class="eyebrow">VOLT.NET / THE SHOWCASE</p><h1>Built with the tool<br />it demonstrates.</h1><p class="lead">An open-source framework showcase, not a portfolio. The pages are .volt templates compiled by Volt's source generator and exported as HTML.</p></div>
<div class="prose"><h2>What runs here</h2><p>The SSG examples are real generated output. Layouts, partials and C# loops run during compilation and export. GitHub Pages serves the resulting files; it does not host a .NET process.</p><h2>What needs a server</h2><p>Counter actions, typed form submissions, SSR, revalidation and metrics need a running application. The static Counter is deliberately disabled. The form walkthrough links to a local handler rather than pretending to submit data.</p><h2>What is experimental</h2><p>The WebAssembly island protocol has a fixture and conformance tests. It is not a general C#-to-WASM build pipeline. Auth/sessions, i18n, streaming SSR and runtime template compilation are listed as planned work in the repository, not capabilities demonstrated here.</p><h2>Performance without a scoreboard</h2><p>This site makes no universal throughput claims. The repository includes allocation gates and BenchmarkDotNet scenarios. Their scope matters: route matching and rendering microbenchmarks do not measure an entire production application.</p><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/Puxxalwl/Volt.NET/blob/main/tests/Volt.Core.Tests/ZeroAllocGateTests.cs">Inspect allocation gate tests</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/Puxxalwl/Volt.NET/tree/main/tests/Volt.Benchmarks">Run the rendering benchmarks</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/Puxxalwl/Volt.NET/tree/main/examples/starter">Start from the real application example</a></li></ul><h2>Inspect the implementation</h2><p>Read <a href="https://github.com/Puxxalwl/Volt.NET/tree/main/apps/demo">the complete showcase source</a>, <a href="https://github.com/Puxxalwl/Volt.NET/tree/main/apps/docs">documentation templates</a> or <a href="https://github.com/Puxxalwl/Volt.NET/blob/main/README.md">the setup guide</a>. No separate frontend framework is used.</p></div>
